  "title": "Why “Online Vehicle Sales” Usually Breaks at Checkout",
  "summary": "Most digital-retail tools — and marketplace “Buy Now” buttons — quietly hand the deal back to the dealer’s back office the moment anything real has to happen. This piece walks through the six places online vehicle sales actually break (financing, stipulations, F&I, tax, titling, signing) in the order they show up in a deal, what each one costs the dealer, and what real checkout-to-keys infrastructure has to absorb instead.",
